[gd_scene load_steps=32 format=3]

; Tandem-axle drawbar TIPPING TRAILER for the tractor. Hand-built low-poly (Kenney ships no
; trailers and no implements at all), flat boxes and 8-10 segment cylinders to match the kit's
; flat-shaded look, exactly like the four semi-trailers and the four three-point implements.
;
; AUTHORED WITH THE ORIGIN AT THE DRAWBAR EYE, ground at y = -0.40 -- measured off the tractor's own
; drawbar pin, which drawbar.tscn puts 0.40 m above the road. THAT DATUM IS NOT THE SEMI-TRAILERS'
; y = -1.05 AND MUST NEVER BE COPIED FROM THEM: -1.05 is a fifth-wheel PLATE height. Making the eye
; the origin is what keeps Articulation.coupled_pose a single transform multiply, and it is the
; implements' convention in the same shape ("origin on the lower pin line, ground at y = -0.21").
;
; THE BODY SITS OVER THE WHEELS, and that is the shape rule here that the gooseneck rule is on a
; semi. There is no plate to clear, so nothing is forced up at the front -- but the 0.36 m wheels
; reach y = 0.32 in this frame, so the frame rails start at y 0.36 and the floor rides at 0.54.
; Authored low instead, like a semi's drop deck, the axles come straight up through the floor.
;
; Sizes are measured against the shipped kit, not against real machinery: the sedan is 1.80 m wide
; and 2.88 long, the tractor 1.60 wide on a 1.57 m wheelbase. So this is 1.90 wide over the body
; with a 3.90 m box, and the whole combination behind the tractor comes to about 7.0 m.
;
; The clearances that are geometry rather than taste:
;   - the frontmost part is the eye at z = -0.05 on the centreline, so nothing swings on more than
;     0.12 m and the SWING STOP is set by the frame's front corners instead: they sit at
;     (|x| 0.66, z 1.15), i.e. 1.33 m from the eye, and reach the tractor's rear tyres only past
;     ~108 deg. Drawbar.SWING_MAX_DEG is 90, and test_drawbar_trailer sweeps every BoxMesh corner
;     of this scene against those tyres rather than trusting that arithmetic.
;   - the tipping body's collision is TWO AUTHORED POSES, never a shape re-transformed per tick --
;     see farm_tipper.gd's _swap_collision. CollisionTipBodyRaised is the SAME BoxShape3D swept
;     TIP_MAX_DEG (45 deg) about the hinge at (0, 0.60, 4.95), so the two cannot disagree by
;     construction. It is not optional: the interlock refuses the RAISE direction only, so driving
;     away with the body up is a pose the world has to be able to hit.
;   - there are no landing legs and no parking jack. A farm trailer is left standing on its own
;     nose, and this one spawns coupled.
;
; Undriven and unsteered: the axles only ever brake. Suspension / mass / grip live in
; farm_tipper_spec.tres, wheels are the kit's own truck wheel scaled on the INSTANCE (RayWheel
; overwrites each Wheels/* root transform every tick, so the scale must ride the child).

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/vehicles/tractor/trailers/farm_tipper.gd" id="1_tipper"]
[ext_resource type="Resource" path="res://src/vehicles/tractor/trailers/farm_tipper_spec.tres" id="2_spec"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://src/vehicles/kenney/wheel-truck.tscn" id="3_wheel"]

