; Wheel visual roots, IN THE SAME ORDER as farm_tipper_spec.tres's wheel_positions (L/R per axle,
; front axle first) -- TowedBody pairs them by index and errors on a count mismatch. RayWheel
; overwrites each root's transform every tick, so the radius scale and the right-side flip ride the
; INSTANCED CHILD. The flip is about Vector3.RIGHT, never UP: in the frame RayWheel builds, the
; wheel's local Y is the AXLE, so a yaw would just spin it about its own axis.
;
; The roots ARE authored at their hubs (0.36 m above this trailer's ground, i.e. y -0.04) even
; though RayWheel overwrites them on the first tick. It costs nothing at runtime and it is what the
; selector card and the editor show: a body that is never ticked -- a frozen display rig -- keeps
; whatever is authored here, and at the default (0, 0, 0) all four wheels stack up at the drawbar
; eye. (The four semi-trailers still do exactly that on their own cards; this is not a rule they
; broke, it is one nobody had written down yet.)
